  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance to Repatriated Migrants in Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While repatriations of Haitian migrants from the U.S. to Haiti had been paused after the devastating earthquake on 14 August, this sudden surge in migrant crossings has prompted it to change course. To prepare for this increase in repatriation movements from the U.S., and given the particular vulnerabilities of Haitian returnees, IOM aims to increase its direct support to the National Migration Office (ONM) to provide direct assistance to returning/repatriated migrants, as well as the Institute for Social Welfare and Research (IBESR) and the Haitian Coast Guard, also involved in the assistance to vulnerable migrants.</narrative>
  </description>
